            <div xml:id="d672">

                <pb facs="0725" n="613" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg613"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/3851 a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Commission to
                        Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-02-08T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 8,
                                1919, 6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>643. For the Secretary of State:</p>
                <p>Secretary of War requests that you will inform the President that War Department,
                    although anxious in regard to the Archangel situation is not giving
                    consideration to the question as to whether the troops there are in any actual
                    danger, nor is it giving consideration to the question as to whether they need
                    reinforcement, as it is his understanding that the American force in Archangel
                    is operating under the command of General Foch, and that the Supreme War Council
                    would therefore be charged with the duty of seeing that it is properly
                    reinforced and in general protecting safety of the various units making up the
                    forces.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
